<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="es">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, maximum-scale=1.0, user-scalable=no">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#6366f1">
  <title>WiFi Gratis</title>
  <!-- Set <base> dynamically so relative URLs resolve under /<slug>/ regardless of the current
       SPA route (e.g. /<slug>/video). Must run before any <link>/<script> below. -->
  <script>
    (function () {
      var slug = location.pathname.split('/').filter(Boolean)[0];
      if (slug && slug !== 'api') {
        var b = document.createElement('base');
        b.href = '/' + slug + '/';
        document.head.appendChild(b);
      }
    })();
  </script>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{CSS_PATH}}">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="./custom-styles.css.gz" onerror="this.remove()">
  <!-- Written by the build, not by hand: the chunk names carry a content hash. Naming them here is
       what lets them be requested together with `main.js` instead of after it has been parsed —
       measured at 119 ms off the critical path with 100 ms of round-trip time.
       Only the eager ones: a route chunk arrives through a dynamic import, and preloading those
       would download every view on the first paint, which is the opposite of why the split is
       there. -->
{{PRELOADS}}
</head>
<body>
  <!-- Fuera de #app y con el mismo markup que el estado de carga de Layout, para que el relevo no
       mueva nada. Lo borra Layout al montar, no un timer: esto es lo unico en pantalla mientras
       bajan main.js y el chunk de la primera vista. -->
  <div class="initial-loader">
    <!-- Sin los <span class="ring-track"> y <span class="ring-arc"> que estaban aca: eran los
         hooks del anillo giratorio que se probo y se descarto. La animacion de espera es `breathe`
         sobre el icono. Quedaban vacios y ocultos por una regla `display: none`, y `BrandLoader`
         -- que renderiza este mismo bloque desde Laminar -- ya no los emitia, asi que el markup
         estatico y el dinamico habian divergido. -->
    <div class="brand-ring">
      <img src="./brand-icon.svg" class="brand-icon" alt="Cargando">
    </div>
  </div>
  <div id="app"></div>
  <!-- `type="module"`: the client links as ES modules so each route can arrive in its own chunk,
       and the browser resolves the imports between them by the exact paths the linker wrote. -->
  <script type="module" src="{{JS_PATH}}"></script>
</body>
</html>
